---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Just Capture">
    <img
        src="/just-capture/logo.png"
        alt="Just Capture app icon"
        width="96"
        height="96"
        style="border-radius: 20px;"
    />
    <h1>Just Capture</h1>

    <p>
        <strong>Record. Back up. Notify.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
        Just Capture is a free iPhone and Android app that records video and tries
        to back it up to your own Google Drive as you record, so your footage isn't
        stored only on your phone. It can also email the people you choose when
        you start recording, with a link to watch.
    </p>
    <p>
        We don't run any servers for Just Capture. Your videos go to your own
        Google Drive, and we never receive them.
    </p>

    <h2>How It Works</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>Sign in with your Google account.</li>
        <li>
            Optionally, add the email addresses of the people you want to notify
            when you start recording.
        </li>
        <li>
            Start recording. The app records in clips of 10, 30, or 60 seconds.
            When each clip ends, the app tries to upload it to a new folder in
            your Google Drive.
        </li>
        <li>
            If you added recipients, the app sends them an email from your Gmail
            account. It includes a link to the Drive folder and, if you choose,
            the time and your location.
        </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
        Clips also stay on your phone. If you lose your connection, the app
        keeps recording and tries the upload again later.
    </p>

    <h2>Features</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Gapless 1080p video recording, split into short clips</li>
        <li>Clip uploads to your Google Drive while you record</li>
        <li>Email notifications with a customizable subject and message</li>
        <li>Optional location trail for each recording, on your phone and in Drive</li>
        <li>Optional start time and location in notification emails</li>
        <li>Replay of your own recordings, whether on your phone or in Drive</li>
        <li>Replay of Drive folders that other people shared with you by link</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why We Ask for Google Access</h2>
    <p>
        Just Capture uses Google Sign-In and asks for these permissions:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Google Drive (only files the app creates or opens)</strong>:
            to create recording folders, upload clips, and play them back. The
            app can't see the rest of your Drive.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Gmail (send email only)</strong>: to send notifications from
            your account to the people you chose. The app can't read your email.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Your email address</strong>: to show which account is signed
            in.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Your name and profile photo (iPhone only)</strong>: to show
            which account is signed in and to tell recipients who started
            recording.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Before You Use It</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Notifying people shares the recording by link.</strong> When
            the app emails your recipients, it sets that recording's Drive
            folder to "Anyone with the link" so that they can open it without
            requesting access. Anyone who gets the link can watch and, if you
            save your location, follow your trail, so share it with care.
            You can change this at any time in Google Drive. If no email is
            sent, the folder stays private.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Uploads aren't guaranteed.</strong> They depend on your
            connection and your available Drive storage.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Just Capture doesn't contact emergency services.</strong> In
            an emergency, call your local emergency number.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Recording laws vary.</strong> You are responsible for
            following the laws where you record, including any rules on
            recording other people.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Requirements</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>An iPhone running iOS 26.5 or later, or an Android device running Android 8.0 or later</li>
        <li>A Google account</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Work and school Google accounts may not allow link sharing. If yours
        doesn't, the people you notify won't be able to open your videos, so we
        recommend a personal Google account.
    </p>
    <p>Just Capture isn't on the App Store or Google Play yet.</p>

    <h2>Privacy and License</h2>
    <p>
        Read our <a href="/just-capture/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> for
        details on how Just Capture handles your data.
    </p>
    <p>
        Just Capture is free and open source under a GPL 3.0 license, and the
        code is available on Github for{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/Just-Free-Software/just-capture-ios">iPhone</a>
        {" "}and{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/Just-Free-Software/just-capture-android">Android</a>.
    </p>
</Layout>
